# Riot (CR 702.136a) under Solemnity ("counters can't be put on creatures", CR 122.6, 101.2): Bot1 casts Solemnity, then
# Zhur-Taa Goblin and chooses the +1/+1 counter. The counter can't be put on it, so it enters with none, and "if a creature
# entering the battlefield has riot but can't have a +1/+1 counter put onto it, it gains haste" (the card's ruling): it
# is a 2/2 with haste and attacks the turn it enters.

